<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">John McCormack</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1906</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording (Johnson's tune)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Our Lady's Choral Society</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1965</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Wolfe Tones</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording (voted top in the BBC World Service poll, 2002)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Dubliners</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording (Johnson's tune)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Winston Churchill's telegram to Éamon de Valera</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1941</span><span class="sg-chain-h">title quoted in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">A Hard Day's Night, film</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung in a scene</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Clarinet Concerto (Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Davis copied his melody from it</span></li></ul></section>
